  "_meta": {
    "notes": "The settings are HONOURED rather than reported, and this is the picture that proves it. Retirement is switched off and mission training with it, so the word retirement appears nowhere on the surface and neither does a lapse date: not an empty cell, not a line saying the mechanic is off. The concepts are absent from the save, so they are absent from the screen. What is left is what this save actually runs, which is proficiency training",
    "why-no-rules-section": "There was a CREW RULES section here restating the five difficulty settings a save differs from RP-1's defaults on. It is gone: a setting is an input to what the surface renders, not content of its own, and an operator who has to read a rule and then apply it to the rows themselves has been handed the job the widget exists to do",
    "why-every-course-is-a-proficiency": "Mission training is switched off, and RP-1 generates a mission template only while it is on (CrewHandler.AddPartCourses), so no mission course can be running on this save. A fixture showing one would be a picture of a state the game cannot reach"
